 "text": "Hey, how are you feeling? Gaugh is a traditional Irish drink, usually made with whiskey, milk, and some sweetness. Kind of, but with a kick of alcohol. You can add fruit or spices to spice it up. It' not too strong, and you can adjust the alcohol by using lower proof whiskey. People often start with a quarter of a cup of milk. The whiskey, then the milk, the sugar, and any fruit or spices. Stir until you're happy with the sweetness. It' easy to adjust to your taste. Some people like it warm and creamy. Exactly. You can pour it over ice too, if you feeling cooler.",
